lur values lower than `0.05` won't cause shadow acne. I've empirically found that values like `0.01` and `0.02` still exhibit acne at some angles, while `0.05` is free of acne at any angle I could test.\r\n\r\nI couldn't find where SpotLight3D bias is adjusted according to blur, so I didn't fix that issue though. The testing project includes an invisible SpotLight3D if you want to help investigate this.\r\n\r\n- This closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/103165.\r\n- See https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/68339 where the bias adjustment was originally added.\r\n\r\n**Testing project:** [test_shadow_bias_blur.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19061937/test_shadow_bias_blur.zip)\r\n\r\n## Preview\r\n\r\nBefore | After\r\n-|-\r\n![Screenshot_20250304_005004](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/57d5fc1e-caa0-48c6-8e2a-68828144309d) | ![Screenshot_20250304_005020](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4dcf8506-c4df-423c-95ce-a286ca073951)\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098111,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgxMTE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:rendering","name":"topic:rendering","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666708289,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA4Mjg5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:3d","name":"topic:3d","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"202